1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,242
A helpful reply should lead to a correct appointment.

2
00:00:03,242 --> 00:00:06,483
Meet How Yue: a patient dental concierge for Taiwan.

3
00:00:06,483 --> 00:00:12,325
It connects everyday language with decisions you can inspect, and changes you must confirm.

4
00:00:12,325 --> 00:00:14,836
This is the live English demo.

5
00:00:14,836 --> 00:00:19,857
Choose a fictional patient and type: not cancel, please reschedule my appointment.

6
00:00:19,857 --> 00:00:24,878
Our fine-tuned NVIDIA four-billion-parameter model scores eight intents in one forward pass.

7
00:00:24,878 --> 00:00:29,062
The panel shows the actual adapter, scores, and processing events.

8
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:33,627
Buttons are simply shortcuts to the same text pipeline.

9
00:00:33,627 --> 00:00:36,837
The model cannot change a booking by itself.

10
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:40,849
Application rules check patient ownership, dates, doctors, availability, and versions.

11
00:00:40,849 --> 00:00:44,059
Select a time, review the proposal, and confirm.

12
00:00:44,059 --> 00:00:47,670
Only then does an atomic transaction update the appointment.

13
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:49,676
Read back the saved result.

14
00:00:49,676 --> 00:00:56,494
If a slot is taken or a confirmation is stale, the original appointment is preserved.

15
00:00:56,494 --> 00:00:58,626
People sometimes click by mistake.

16
00:00:58,626 --> 00:01:01,185
Explicit confusion gets patient, step-by-step guidance.

17
00:01:01,185 --> 00:01:06,729
Repeating the same request keeps the pending choice and skips another model call.

18
00:01:06,729 --> 00:01:09,715
We do not guess a person’s age.

19
00:01:09,715 --> 00:01:14,780
Supportive language uses transparent rules, not a trained emotion classifier.

20
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:18,444
A request for a person opens a real handoff case.

21
00:01:18,444 --> 00:01:22,475
The assistant does not pretend that a staff member has replied.

22
00:01:22,475 --> 00:01:25,773
Symptoms and family bookings also follow conservative handoff rules.

23
00:01:25,773 --> 00:01:28,405
All patients here are synthetic.

24
00:01:28,405 --> 00:01:34,719
Below a score of zero point eight five, or when local inference is unavailable, NVIDIA Nano

25
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:38,270
thirty B on Nebius Token Factory provides budgeted fallback.

26
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:39,848
Supabase commits the transaction.

27
00:01:39,848 --> 00:01:44,189
Tavily supports staff research, with human approval before knowledge is used.

28
00:01:44,189 --> 00:01:47,751
The app and database run in Tokyo.

29
00:01:47,751 --> 00:01:51,419
We trained the adapter on an NVIDIA L four.

30
00:01:51,419 --> 00:01:57,532
On a fixed sixty-four-item synthetic test, the base scored fifty-two correct and the adapter fifty-eight.

31
00:01:57,532 --> 00:02:00,385
One accepted high-score prediction was still wrong.

32
00:02:00,385 --> 00:02:05,276
The warmed local median was fifty-three milliseconds, excluding network and database time.

33
00:02:05,276 --> 00:02:08,929
These are engineering measurements, not clinical validation.

34
00:02:08,929 --> 00:02:12,313
The primary training language is Taiwanese Mandarin.

35
00:02:12,313 --> 00:02:16,664
English is interactive too, with separately documented smoke tests.

36
00:02:16,664 --> 00:02:21,982
The code, adapter, full training recipe, failures, and costs are public.

37
00:02:21,982 --> 00:02:24,399
How Yue: understand, confirm, complete.

38
00:02:24,399 --> 00:02:27,133
Try the live demo.
